Note: 57/100 kills here vs. 49/100 in the Phase 5 run — the RNG seed is
identical (0xFA07_1E5EC0FFEE); which iterations actually land a kill depends
on real wall-clock timing against Python/PyTorch startup and the forward
pass itself, not on the seed alone, and CF_COMMIT_META's extra (small)
serialize-and-stage work shifts that timing slightly. A different kill
count between runs of equivalent code is expected non-determinism in the
race, not a regression — the invariant that matters (0 non-atomic states)
held regardless.

Note: this run was preceded by an earlier same-day attempt whose process
output was lost to a session interruption before it could be transcribed,
despite the underlying `cargo test` process itself completing successfully
in the background (exit code 0, both tests passed, 0 non-atomic states in
both arms). That earlier run is not cited here because its exact kill
counts were not captured before the interruption; this run's numbers are
what is cited in docs/benchmark_report.md and README.md. Total wall-clock
time for both arms in this run was 3823.67s —
elevated versus Phase 5's 2001.51s baseline for the same reason
phase5_fault_injection.log's own note describes (shared hardware, other
work in the session), not a hang or a performance regression in the commit
